---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Taskship · From task to agent, in one command">
  <main class="landing">
    <section class="hero">
      <div class="eyebrow">Developer tools, without the busywork</div>
      <h1>From task to agent,<br /><span>in one command.</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Taskship is a local-first task manager and agent dispatcher. Organize work on your own
        terms, then hand a task to your coding agent with the context it needs to get started.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn primary" href="/docs/quickstart/">Read the quickstart →</a>
        <a class="btn" href="/docs/concepts/">How it works</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="terminal">
      <div class="termbar">
        <div class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
        <span>terminal · taskship</span>
        <span></span>
      </div>
      <pre><span class="dim"># Pick a task. Launch an agent.</span>
<span class="cmd">$ taskship PROJ-42</span>

<span class="good">✓</span> Resolved task <b>PROJ-42</b>
<span class="good">✓</span> Project: myproject
<span class="good">✓</span> Workspace: ~/code/myproject
<span class="good">✓</span> Starting Claude with task context

<span class="dim">Agent: I'll inspect the repository, assess the
requirements, and propose a plan before coding.</span></pre>
    </div>

    <section class="sectionhead">
      <h2>Built for the way developers work</h2>
      <p>A complete task manager on its own. An agent dispatcher when you need one.</p>
    </section>
    <div class="cards">
      <article class="card">
        <span class="ico">▤</span>
        <h3>Manage tasks anywhere</h3>
        <p>
          Projects, priorities, descriptions, and acceptance criteria. Start locally with
          SQLite, with no server or account needed.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="ico">↗</span>
        <h3>Dispatch with context</h3>
        <p>
          Launch Claude directly from a task. The agent reviews requirements, inspects the repo,
          and proposes a plan first.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <span class="ico">⌘</span>
        <h3>Own your workflow</h3>
        <p>
          Work in the CLI or TUI. Add a self-hosted backend for multiple machines, and connect
          external trackers later.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
